statement:
Fix a prime $\ell$, an algebraic closure $\Omega$ of $\mathbf Q_\ell$, and a finite intermediate field $E$ with its $\ell$-adic norm topology [def-weil-l-adic-coefficient-extension]. Let $r\geq0$ and let $L=\mathbf Z_\ell^r$ with its inverse-limit topology. A representation here means a finite-dimensional $E$-vector space $W$ with its usual norm topology and a jointly continuous $E$-linear action of $L$ [def-pod-l-adic-representations]. Write $T_i(W)$ for the action of $1$ in the $i$th factor, for $1\leq i\leq r$. Let $P$ be a property of these representations invariant under equivariant $E$-linear isomorphisms. Suppose:
(i) $P(W)$ holds for every trivial representation, including $W=0$;
(ii) $P(W)$ holds whenever $T_i(W)-\mathrm{id}_W$ is invertible for at least one $i$;
(iii) for every $L$-stable subspace $U\subseteq W$, with the induced continuous representations on $U$ and $W/U$, the implication $P(U)\ \text{and}\ P(W/U)\Rightarrow P(W)$ holds.
Then $P(W)$ holds for every such continuous representation $W$. This includes $r=0$, when the family of operators is empty.
